    "result_text": "The build is green. All changes are complete and the test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the derived string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) assigned at creation.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string, GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) response field with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3, readOnly). The generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membershipLevel` (`Integer`, column `membership_level`) with getter/setter, following the existing pattern of creation-time fields (`namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber`, etc.).\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `membership_level INTEGER` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the read-time `membershipTier` derivation expression. `membershipLevel` now maps straight through by name.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `assignMembershipLevel(owner)` in the create flow (after `assignNamesakeCount`, so the count is settled): starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Updated the create **audit line** to record `membershipLevel=\u2026` instead of the tier, plus corresponding doc comments (including removing the now-stale GOLD-tier reference on `assignHouseholdMembership`).\n\nThe new `coreNumericLevel` acceptance test (owner with an email and a unique name \u2192 level `1 + email + namesake0 = 3`) passes, and the audit output confirms `membershipLevel=3` is recorded.",
